# Greenfield Threat Hunt Investigation Report

**Incident ID:** GF-INC-2026-0704  
**Investigator:** Andrew Gay  
**Investigation Type:** Threat Hunt / Incident Response  
**Environment:** Greenfield Lab  
**Tools Used:** Microsoft Defender XDR, Microsoft Sentinel, PowerShell, Windows 11 Analysis VM

---

# Executive Summary

A threat hunt was conducted within the Greenfield environment after suspicious endpoint activity was identified on **GF-WS01**. The investigation focused on identifying the initial compromise, reconstructing the attack timeline, analyzing recovered malware artifacts, and assessing the overall impact.

Analysis of a recovered HTML file (`blog_lure.html`) identified a hidden prompt injection that instructed the execution of a malicious PowerShell command. Static analysis of the associated PowerShell loader (`loader.ps1`) confirmed an AMSI bypass, download of an XOR-encoded payload, and in-memory shellcode execution using Windows API functions.

Microsoft Defender XDR telemetry confirmed outbound HTTPS communications from both **chrome.exe** and **powershell.exe** to attacker-controlled infrastructure (`cdn.cloud-endpoint.net`). Additional activity included KeePass execution and WMI authentication events. Although malicious execution was confirmed, no evidence of persistence, successful credential theft, or data exfiltration was identified during the investigation.

The incident was assessed as **High Severity** due to successful malware execution and external command-and-control communication.

